<h2><%= SparcConfig.app_name %> could not grant access your identity provider asked for</h2>

<p>
  In the last <%= @window_hours %> hours,
  <strong><%= @total_users %> <%= "user".pluralize(@total_users) %></strong>
  signed in carrying a grant that names something this instance does not have.
</p>

<p>
  They were signed in successfully and keep whatever access did resolve.
  Nothing was created — creating an organization or boundary from a claim would
  let the identity provider define the estate.
</p>

<table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 1px solid #999;">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="text-align: left; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #999;">Reason</th>
      <th style="text-align: right; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #999;">Users</th>
      <th style="text-align: right; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #999;">Sign-ins</th>
      <th style="text-align: left; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #999;">Example grant</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @summary.each do |row| %>
      <tr>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #999;"><%= row[:reason] %></td>
        <td style="text-align: right; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #999;"><%= row[:affected_users] %></td>
        <td style="text-align: right; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #999;"><%= row[:occurrences] %></td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #999;"><code><%= row[:example_grant] %></code></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>What to do</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    If the organization, boundary or role <strong>should</strong> exist, create it.
    The grant resolves by itself at the user's next sign-in — there is nothing to clear.
  </li>
  <li>
    If it should not, the group is misnamed in your identity provider. Correct it there.
  </li>
</ul>

<p>Full detail, including who was affected and when, is in the admin area under
   <strong>IdP Grants</strong>.</p>

<p><small>You are receiving this because you are an administrator of this instance.</small></p>
